:: Nursery encounter - visiting parent [bg-guesthouse]
<h1 class="ptitle">GUEST HOUSE</h1>
<br /><br />
/* A caretaker brings a child to see their parents at the guest house. The player can join in, and it matters more if the child is his. */
<<set _enc = setup.nurseryEncounters>>
<<set _cast = _enc.cast()>>
<<if !_cast>>
	<<goto 'Guest house'>>
<<else>>
<<set _carer = _cast.carer>>
<<set _kid = _cast.kid>>
<<set _mother = _cast.mother ?? null>>
<<set _father = _cast.father ?? null>>
<<set _parents = [_mother, _father].filter(Boolean)>>
<<set _parent = _parents[0]>>
<<set _name = setup.displayName(_carer)>>
<<set _parentNames = _enc.names(_parents)>>
<<set _heOrShe = setup.pronounceWhat(_carer)>>
<<set _kidHe = setup.pronounceWhat(_kid)>>
<<set _kidHis = setup.pronounceWhos(_kid)>>
<<set _kidHim = setup.pronounceWho(_kid)>>
<<set _age = setup.getAge(_kid)>>
<<set _own = _enc.isOwnChild(_kid)>>
<<set _parentWord = _mother && _father ? 'parents' : _mother ? 'mom' : 'dad'>>
/* These happen whatever the player does */
<<set _visitEffects = function () {
	_parents.forEach(npc => {
		_enc.change(npc, 'happy', 2, 5);
		_enc.changeBetween(_carer, npc, 2, 4);
	});
	_enc.change(_kid, 'happy', 2, 5);
}>>

<<if _age < 2>>
	You are crossing the guest house when <<=_name>> comes through the door with <<=_kid.name>> on one hip, looking for <<=_parentNames>>. <<=ucfirst(setup.pronounceWhat(_parent))>> is on <<=setup.pronounceWhos(_parent)>> feet with <<=setup.pronounceWhos(_parent)>> arms out before <<=_name>> has made it halfway across the room.
	<br /><br />
	<<sayNpc _carer>>
		Somebody has been fussing for you all day, and I thought we could both use the walk. There you go. See? I told you <<=_parentWord === 'parents' ? 'they were' : (_parentWord === 'mom' ? 'she was' : 'he was')>> here.
	<</sayNpc>>
	<br />
	<<=_kid.name>> grabs a fistful of <<=setup.displayName(_parent)>>'s shirt and goes quiet at once.
<<elseif _age < 13>>
	You are crossing the guest house when the door bangs open and <<=_kid.name>> runs in ahead of <<=_name>>, who is doing <<=setup.pronounceWhos(_carer)>> best to keep up.
	<br /><br />
	<<set _mom = _age < 13 ? 'mommy' : 'mom'>>
	<<set _dad = _age < 13 ? 'daddy' : 'dad'>>
	<<set _afterClass = _enc.currentSlot() === 'afterSchool' && _age >= 5 && ($player.quests.school_built ?? false)>>
	"I found <<=_parentWord === 'parents' ? _mom + ' and ' + _dad : (_parentWord === 'mom' ? _mom : _dad)>>!" <<=_kidHe>> shouts, and throws <<=_kidHim>>self at <<=_parentNames>>.
	<br /><br />
	<<sayNpc _carer>>
		<<=ucfirst(_kidHe)>> has been asking to come over since <<=_afterClass ? 'school let out' : 'breakfast'>>. We finished up early, so I said we could stop by for a little while.
	<</sayNpc>>
<<else>>
	You are crossing the guest house when <<=_name>> comes in with <<=_kid.name>>, who is trying to look as though this wasn't <<=_kidHis>> idea. <<=_parentNames>> <<=_parents.length > 1 ? 'look up and break' : 'looks up and breaks'>> into a smile.
	<br /><br />
	<<sayNpc _carer>>
		I had an errand this way, and this one offered to carry for me. I don't think it was the carrying <<=_kidHe>> had in mind.
	<</sayNpc>>
	<br />
	<<=_kid.name>> rolls <<=_kidHis>> eyes and sits down anyway, close enough for <<=_parentNames>> to reach over and muss <<=_kidHis>> hair.
<</if>>
<br /><br />
<<if _own>>
	<<=_kid.name>> is your own <<=[0, 2].includes(_kid.gender) ? 'daughter' : 'son'>>. <<=setup.displayName(_parent)>> catches your eye across the room, and <<=setup.pronounceWhat(_parent)>> nods toward the empty place beside <<=setup.pronounceWho(_parent)>>.
<<else>>
	<<=_name>> notices you standing there and gives you a little wave, leaving room on the bench if you care to sit.
<</if>>
<br /><br />

<div id="nce_choices">
	<<link 'Sit down and join them (Uses 30 minutes)'>>
		<<replace '#nce_choices'>>
			<<run _visitEffects()>>
			<<addmins 30>>
			<<run [_carer, _kid].concat(_parents).forEach(npc => _enc.change(npc, 'relationship', 2, 3))>>
			<<if _own>>
				<<run _enc.change(_kid, 'relationship', 2, 4)>>
				<<if _mother>><<run _enc.change(_mother, 'relationship', 2, 4)>><</if>>
			<</if>>
			You put aside what you came to do and sit down with them. For half an hour nobody needs a decision from you, and nobody is asking about food or fuel or who is on watch tonight.
			<br /><br />
			<<if _age < 2>>
				<<=_kid.name>> is passed into your arms at some point, and studies your face with enormous suspicion before falling asleep on your chest.
			<<elseif _age < 13>>
				<<=_kid.name>> tells you a long story with several parts missing, and you ask all the right questions. By the end <<=_kidHe>> has climbed onto the bench beside you as if <<=_kidHe>> has always sat there.
			<<else>>
				<<=_kid.name>> doesn't say much at first, but you ask what <<=_kidHe>> has been up to and actually listen to the answer. By the end <<=_kidHe>> is arguing with you about it, and enjoying <<=_kidHim>>self.
			<</if>>
			<br /><br />
			<<if _own>>
				<<=setup.displayName(_parent)>> leans into your shoulder and doesn't say anything for a while.
				<br /><br />
				<<sayNpc _parent>>
					This is the part I like to remember when this life gets difficult. Thank you for staying, and reminding me of the father you can be for <<=_kidHim>>.
				<</sayNpc>>
			<<else>>
				<<=_parentNames>> and <<=_name>> both look a little surprised at how easily you fit in.
				<br /><br />
				<<sayNpc _carer>>
					I'll have to get this one back soon. But I'm glad you sat down. People don't see this side of you often enough.
				<</sayNpc>>
			<</if>>
			<br />
			[[Continue|Guest house]]
			<<nurseryEffects>>
		<</replace>>
	<</link>>
	<<link 'Leave them to it'>>
		<<replace '#nce_choices'>>
			<<run _visitEffects()>>
			<<if _own>>
				<<run _enc.change(_kid, 'relationship', -5, -5)>>
				<<run _enc.change(_kid, 'happy', -5, -5)>>
				<<if _mother>><<run _enc.change(_mother, 'relationship', -5, -5)>><</if>>
				You tell them you have too much to do and head for the door. The smile on <<=setup.displayName(_parent)>>'s face goes away slowly.
				<br /><br />
				<<sayNpc _parent>>
					Of course. You're busy. You always are.
				<</sayNpc>>
				<br />
				<<if _age >= 2>>
					<<=_kid.name>> watches you go and doesn't say anything. <<=_name>> pulls <<=_kidHim>> a little closer and starts talking about something else.
				<<else>>
					<<=_kid.name>> reaches a hand after you, then forgets about it. <<=setup.displayName(_parent)>> doesn't.
				<</if>>
			<<else>>
				You nod to them and leave them to their visit. Behind you, <<=_name>> settles on the bench while <<=_parentNames>> <<=_parents.length > 1 ? 'fuss' : 'fusses'>> over <<=_kid.name>>, and the room feels a little warmer for it.
			<</if>>
			<br /><br />
			[[Continue|Guest house]]
			<<nurseryEffects>>
		<</replace>>
	<</link>>
</div>
<</if>>
